]},
{"clause_id": "c033", "issues": [
  {"issue": "The final sentence withholds coverage for \"any loss arising from any act or omission by an Insured Person's estate, heirs, legal representatives, assigns, or spouse,\" which may take back the very coverage the subsection grants. Where the grant ends and the carve-out begins is unclear.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
]},
{"clause_id": "c034", "issues": [
  {"issue": "This coverage is deleted for the Brokerage/Advisory, Fiduciary and Securities Liability Insuring Agreements by paragraph 2.A of Endorsements 5091, 5093 and 5098. Whether any Not-for-Profit Directorship coverage survives across the Policy as a whole must be read from those endorsements.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
]},
{"clause_id": "c035", "issues": [
  {"issue": "The right to purchase is triggered by conversion only \"subject to Section XIII (C)(1)(b),\" but Section XIII (C)(2) says the occurrence of ANY of the conversion events in (C)(1) — including Financial Impairment under (C)(1)(a) — shall not affect the right to purchase the Discovery Period. The two provisions give different triggers.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.34}
]},
{"clause_id": "c036", "issues": [
  {"issue": "The Discovery Period covers Wrongful Acts occurring before \"the effective date of cancellation, nonrenewal or conversion,\" while the amended Section IV (E) in the Discovery Period Endorsement uses \"prior to the termination date of this Policy\" as its cut-off. Which date limits the covered Wrongful Acts is left unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26}
]},
{"clause_id": "c037", "issues": [
  {"issue": "The premium formula multiplies the Item 10(a) annual premium by the Item 4 percentage, but the Discovery Period Activation Endorsement instead sets out its own fixed premium figures per Insuring Agreement. Which controls if they diverge is not addressed.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
]},
{"clause_id": "c038", "issues": [
  {"issue": "The sixty-day lapse period runs from \"the effective date of such cancellation, nonrenewal or conversion,\" but conversion under Section XIII (C) is an event with no stated effective date or notice. When the clock starts on a conversion is therefore uncertain.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
]},
{"clause_id": "c039", "issues": [
  {"issue": "The Discovery Period limit is made part of the immediately preceding Policy Year's Item 8 limit, yet the Discovery Period Activation Endorsement lists fresh per-Agreement limits ($10,000,000 D&O, $5,000,000 etc.) for the Discovery Period. Whether the Discovery Period has its own limits or shares the expiring year's is the conflict.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
]},
{"clause_id": "c040", "issues": [
  {"issue": "\"Terms, conditions, Limits of Liability, retentions, or premiums different from those applicable to the expiring Policy\" sets no ceiling, so any renewal offer however onerous defeats the Discovery Period right. The boundary of a qualifying \"offer\" is undefined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
]},
{"clause_id": "c041", "issues": [
  {"issue": "\"All applications, attachments and materials submitted to the Insurer\" for this or any predecessor policy is unbounded, and it is not said what \"materials\" means or how far back \"indirect renewal or replacement\" reaches. That matters because Section XV makes those materials the basis of the Policy.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
]},
{"clause_id": "c042", "issues": [
